BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Balconettes
DTSTART:20250519T221500Z
DTEND:20250520T001000Z
DTSTAMP:20250519T221500Z
UID:VOk44RQ1rb
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nNoémie Merlant (Portrait of a L
 ady on Fire) co-writes\, directs\, and stars in this genre-bending feminis
 t comic thriller\, as a trio of Marseille roommates—a camgirl\, a writer
 \, and an actress—rage against toxic masculinity in the middle of a terr
 ible heat wave. Get your girls together for a little excitement with a cha
 nce to win passes to HUMP! Part Two at the May 18 screening and horror-the
 med prizes from the 48 Hour Film Project at the May 19 screening. Sponsore
 d by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-balconettes
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tinā
DTSTART:20250520T010000Z
DTEND:20250520T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T010000Z
UID:EYvAWVr4Kl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 124 mins (2h04m)\n\nFrom Miki Magasiva (SIFF 2024’
 s Indigenous anthology film We Are Still Here) comes this heartfelt and tu
 neful underdog story about Mareta\, a grieving Samoan teacher who finds a 
 new lease on life and connection to community when she forms a student cho
 ir at a wealthy school. Director Miki Magasiva and subject Beulah Koale sc
 heduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/tina
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Viktor
DTSTART:20250520T043000Z
DTEND:20250520T061000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T043000Z
UID:YN7LIxdx1B
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nWhen Russia invaded Ukraine\, Vik
 tor Korotovskyi rallied to join the military but was rejected due to his d
 eafness. Instead\, he became a war photographer. Join Viktor on the frontl
 ines in this wholly immersive and terrifying documentary from producer Dar
 ren Aronofsky. Attend the May 17 screening for a chance to win a book of s
 tunning Ukrainian photography\, courtesy of Ukraine Defense Support. Spons
 ored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/viktor\n\nFilm is also being str
 eamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Undercover
DTSTART:20250520T223000Z
DTEND:20250521T004000Z
DTSTAMP:20250520T223000Z
UID:JAXyabLM4Q
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nA young policewoman is recruited
  to infiltrate the terrorist group ETA and dismantle one of their dangerou
 s commandos. The 2025 Goya Award winner for Best Film recreates an unknow
 n\, shocking\, and terrible true story that offers a testimony to dark and
  violent times that still ripple through today’s Spain. This film is gen
 erously sponsored by Dale Pratt. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fes
 tival/undercover
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SIFF & CFC Present The Dark Crystal with DJ NicFit
DTSTART:20250521T013000Z
DTEND:20250521T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T013000Z
UID:ZyCoWJibT5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nJoin the Gelflings (and Fizzgig!)
  on their quest to defeat the evil Skeksis in this very special presentati
 on of The Dark Crystal. This time\, Seattle’s own DJ NicFit will create 
 a live soundtrack to accompany Jim Henson and Frank Oz’s cult 1982 fanta
 sy adventure. Classified Cinema will be giving out stickers and film poste
 rs made exclusively for this one-time-only event in the lobby before the s
 how! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/siff-and-cfc-present-t
 he-dark-crystal-with-dj-nicfit
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Riefenstahl
DTSTART:20250521T040000Z
DTEND:20250521T061000Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T040000Z
UID:kERnfFfUbP
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA gripping portrait of controver
 sial filmmaker and propagandist Leni Riefenstahl (The Triumph of the Will)
 \, who despite all evidence to the contrary still maintained she was not c
 omplicit in the atrocities carried out by the Third Reich. Sponsored by:\n
 \nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/riefenstahl\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIF
 F Cinema Uptown House 1 (Thu 22 May\, 12:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250521T220000Z
DTEND:20250522T000500Z
DTSTAMP:20250521T220000Z
UID:7iAUDv91vh
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals. Before the screening\, stop by the lobby to explore merch and mater
 ials from Offbeat Films production company and learn more about their crea
 tive work. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/40-acres
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Suburban Fury
DTSTART:20250522T010000Z
DTEND:20250522T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T010000Z
UID:Tly2yaX25q
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 118 mins (1h58m)\n\nLocal documentarian Robinson Dev
 or (Zoo\, Pow Wow) returns to SIFF with this outré and probing biography 
 of Sara Jane Moore\, the FBI informant and single mother who tried to assa
 ssinate President Gerald Ford in 1975\, as told in her own words. Director
  Robinson Devor\, producer Jason Reid\, executive producer/head archivist 
 Bob Fink\, and co-producer Matt Levinthal scheduled to attend. RSVP to joi
 n Seattle Documentary Association for a happy hour celebrating local docum
 entary filmmaking at Sound Hotel directly before the film. Limited space a
 vailable. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/suburban-fury\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1 (Fri 23 May\, 3:30 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diciannove
DTSTART:20250522T041500Z
DTEND:20250522T061500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T041500Z
UID:HQxHpetlDF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nIn this freewheeling Gen Z bildu
 ngsroman co-produced by Luca Guadagnino\, aimless 19-year-old Leonardo lea
 ves his privileged world and economic studies behind to bustle around Sien
 a in desperate search of identity and connection. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:/
 /www.siff.net/festival/diciannove
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:U Are the Universe
DTSTART:20250522T193000Z
DTEND:20250522T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T193000Z
UID:BxMxNEbOLt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nIn this Ukraine-shot tale of fin
 ding connection under the most devastating and isolating of circumstances\
 , a space trucker thinks he’s the last living person in the universe…u
 ntil a call from a distant space station sets him on a course across the c
 osmos. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/u-are-the-universe\n
 \nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema Downtown (Sun 25 May\, 4:15 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Cranko
DTSTART:20250522T220000Z
DTEND:20250523T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250522T220000Z
UID:QwRkifML8m
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 135 mins (2h15m)\n\nSam Riley (Control) stuns in thi
 s biopic about South African dancer and choreographer John Cranko\, who ov
 ercame self-destructive habits and homophobic persecution as he whipped th
 e 1960s Stuttgart Ballet into an internationally renowned dance company. J
 oin Seattle Speaks German for an informal meetup at Cloudburst Brewing bef
 ore the May 23 screening! At 5:00pm\, the conversation starts in German\, 
 and at 5:45pm\, we’ll walk to the theater together. Open to all! If you 
 love queer cinema\, you'll love the chance to win tickets to the Queer & T
 rans Film Festival\, also at the May 23 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps:
 //www.siff.net/festival/john-cranko\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema
  Downtown (Fri 23 May\, 6:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sally
DTSTART:20250523T010000Z
DTEND:20250523T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T010000Z
UID:ERE6MDccbd
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nAward-winning documentarian Cris
 tina Costantini directs this peek into the personal life of Sally Ride\, t
 he first American woman in space. But as Ride journeyed among the stars\, 
 she kept a nearly three-decade romance with author and tennis player Tam O
 ’Shaughnessy a secret. Before the May 22 screening\, stop by the Museum 
 of Flight’s table to learn about their upcoming Sally’s Day celebratio
 n in June. If you’re lucky\, you might even win a pair of museum passes.
  Sponsored by:        This film is also generously sponsored by the No
 vasio-Wilson Community Fund.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/sally\n\nAls
 o playing at:\n  • Shoreline CC Theater (Wed 21 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Souleymane’s Story
DTSTART:20250523T034500Z
DTEND:20250523T053000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T034500Z
UID:ClUjIqsmTX
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nGuinean immigrant Souleymane has 
 applied for asylum in France. Soon he’ll have an interview with the gove
 rnment agency that will change his life…if only he can figure out the ri
 ght story to tell. This film is generously sponsored by Mike Weidemann in 
 memory of Tove Lund and Bruce Hawley. Also sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/souleymanes-story\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • SIFF Cinema D
 owntown (Sat 24 May\, 12:00 PM)\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sanatorium Under the Sign of the Hourglass
DTSTART:20250523T200000Z
DTEND:20250523T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T200000Z
UID:AiPCxm042Y
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 76 mins (1h16m)\n\nThe Brothers Quay spin another fa
 ntastical stop motion yarn with this surreal story inspired by the work of
  Polish writer Bruno Schulz\, about a young man on a ghostly train ride to
 ward a sanatorium that may exist out of time and space. Sponsored by:\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/festival/sanatorium-under-the-sign-of-the-hourglass
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Botanist
DTSTART:20250523T223000Z
DTEND:20250524T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250523T223000Z
UID:8hQolSMkdi
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nIn Jing Yi’s fantastical\, lush
 ly framed drama set in rural northwestern China\, a lonely 13-year-old Kaz
 akh boy in touch with the wonders of nature befriends a local Han girl\, o
 nly for the call of the modern outside world to come calling. Sponsored by
 :\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-botanist\n\nAlso playing at:\n  •
  Shoreline CC Theater (Sat 24 May\, 6:00 PM)
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
